"P803047399" "I Lost my Daddy!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LostKidnappers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2938600522" "'I was so scared...'"
// DetailString :
"P627714461" "As you talked to her, Penelope's tough tomboy facade cracked and all her fears came pouring out as she told you of the night her father was kidnapped and how she escaped only because of an unexpected kindness from the Clockwork: <br><br>'It all started after Dad re-opened the store. These weird guys started hanging around the place. I mean, weirder than normal, and we used to sell groceries to Hero teams, so I know weird. Then one night, those weird guys broke in as we were closing up. They grabbed me and Dad and took us into the sewers. I couldn't tell what they were thinking and I was so scared. Then they ran into a bunch of Clockwork and started fighting. They were doing everything they could to keep me quiet, but I was still able to ask the Clockwork to help and they did. But those weird guys, the Lost, they still got away with my dad. I haven't seen him or heard from him since."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TemblorData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3546366808" "Supergroup database"
// DetailString :
"P3897595367" "This is some old data from one of the ruined Superhero bases scattered throughout Faultline. It clearly shows that Bill Temblor, the secret identity of the villain Faultline, had a cover job where he worked with numerous Heroes as an advisor on scientific and mutant investigations. Investigations where he often ended up foiling his supposed villainous co-conspirators like the Demon Digger and Psicurse. Apparently, Bill Temblor was such a good friend to the city's Heroes that there are records of Heroes taking care of his son, Jim. It doesn't seem to match the maniac who destroyed Overbrook at all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MuxleyLoc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2047513821" "Muxley's location."
// DetailString :
"P1727478304" "One of the defeated Lost told you the location of Muxley, one of their leaders. He told you Muxley was hiding out in an abandoned floor of an old office building. He didn't know the address, but you can figure out where to go."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WhyYins 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3134030844" "'Then it called to us...'"
// DetailString :
"P226772628" "After you defeated Muxley, he told you where you might be able to find Mr. Yin. He also told you why the Lost had tried to abduct the Yins in the first place: <br><br>'We came to the ruins first because the time is near and we feel it in the waters here. But then it called to us. It wants to be used again. The ones marked by the Spider-Lord seek it for their master, and for their own desires. The pirates of the air seek it only because they know it is valuable. We seek it to help bring about the new world. When it comes to light, it will need a new master, a new source of power. The old man is only for control over the girl. There is a reason the Brain-in-Brass protects her.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3477465462" "I Lost my Daddy!"
// DetailString :
"P2376798276" "It all began when Jim Temblor asked you to help out a friend of his, a girl named Penelope Yin.  Penelope's father, Wu Yin, had run Yin's Market before the Faultline Incident and now that the city was rebuilding, they'd returned to reopen.  Unfortunately, the Lost had taken an interest in them and tried to kidnap both Penelope and her father.  Penelope had escaped due to the interference of some Clockwork, but her father was still in the clutches of the Lost.  Penelope had been asking around and learned that the famous Hero historian, Dr. Delilah Stein, might have uncovered something but was now cornered by the Vahzilok!  You battled through the mad murderists to help Doc Delilah, who went to help Penelope.  She also gave you some files she'd uncovered in an abandoned Hero base revealing that Bill Temblor, the secret identity of the villain Faultline, had often helped Heroes against villains with his scientific acumen.  You took that information to Jim Temblor who seemed able to confirm it, further muddying the waters of history."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2895623775" "It all began when Jim Temblor asked you to help out a friend of his, a girl named Penelope Yin.  Penelope's father, Wu Yin, had run Yin's Market before the Faultline Incident and now that the city was rebuilding, they'd returned to reopen.  Unfortunately, the Lost had taken an interest in them and tried to kidnap both Penelope and her father.  Penelope had escaped due to the interference of some Clockwork, but her father was still in the clutches of the Lost.  Penelope had been asking around and learned that the famous Hero historian, Dr. Delilah Stein, might have uncovered something, but was now cornered by the Vahzilok!  You battled through the mad murderists to help Doc Delilah, who went to help Penelope.  She also gave you some files she'd uncovered in an abandoned Hero base revealing that Bill Temblor, the secret identity of the villain Faultline, had often helped Heroes against villains with his scientific acumen.  You took that information to Jim Temblor who seemed able to confirm it, further muddying the waters of history. <br><br>Doc Delilah told Penelope that the Lost headman who had tried to kidnap her and her father was named 'Muxley'.  You hit the streets for information and were soon able to find where Muxley was hiding out.  While Penelope's father wasn't there, Muxley did tell you where you might be able to find him.  He also implied some things about Penelope and what the Lost were doing in Faultline, but wouldn't say more."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL3_FL_Penelope_Yin_MiniArc1_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2182093350" "Yin's market super-saver card"
// tDetailString :
"P1590731343" "Before the Faultline Incident, Yin's Market sold groceries to citizen and Hero alike, and many Heroes with their bases in Overbrook had one of these frequent customer cards.  Now that Yin's Market has re-opened, it might be handy to keep your new Yin's Market card around.  Mr. Yin might never have been rescued if it wasn't for his daughter, Penelope, who told you: <br><br>'I Lost my Daddy!' <br><br>It all began when Jim Temblor asked you to help out a friend of his, a girl named Penelope Yin.  Penelope's father, Wu Yin, had run Yin's Market before the Faultline Incident and now that the city was rebuilding, they'd returned to reopen.  Unfortunately, the Lost had taken an interest in them and tried to kidnap both Penelope and her father.  Penelope had escaped due to the interference of some Clockwork, but her father was still in the clutches of the Lost.  Penelope had been asking around and learned that the famous hero historian, Dr. Delilah Stein, might have uncovered something, but was now cornered by the Vahzilok!  You battled through the mad murderists to help Doc Delilah, who went to help Penelope.  She also gave you some files she'd uncovered in an abandoned Hero base revealing that Bill Temblor, the secret identity of the villain Faultline, had often helped Heroes against villains with his scientific acumen.  You took that information to Jim Temblor, who seemed able to confirm it, further muddying the waters of history. <br><br>Doc Delilah told Penelope that the Lost headman who had tried to kidnap her and her father was named 'Muxley'.  You hit the streets for information and were soon able to find where Muxley was hiding out.  While Penelope's father wasn't there, Muxley did tell you where you might be able to find him.  He also implied some things about Penelope and what the Lost were doing in Faultline, but wouldn't say more. <br><br>With Wu Yin's location, you assaulted a conclave of Lost leaders from all over the city and got Mr. Yin to safety.  Penelope was overjoyed at your success, and Mr. Yin soon re-opened Yin's Market again. <br><br>Though the incident ended on a happy note, there were still some questions left unanswered: what was the thing the Lost were looking for, and why did they think they'd need to control Penelope Yin once they'd found it?  And the information Doc Delilah had discovered about Bill Temblor's heroic efforts to fight villainy conflicted with his actions in his secret identity as Faultline.  If the answers lie in the ruins of the zone, perhaps the person to talk to is the adventuring amazon archeologist, Doc Delilah."

